A||||5||86SE||Will a bad (slow) starter cause it not to start?||||1||
Z||000000||86SE||06-02-2000||02:01 PM||||Just wonderin because I took out my battery from my V-6 and put it in a 2m4 and it still turns over slow.   And I know the battery is good, my v-6 turns over really fast!<P>The engine gets a good spark and gas, so if I get a new starter will it start?||||reg||1
Z||000001||lennyb4||06-02-2000||02:06 PM||||Yep...It sure could. Have you checked the connections on the starter yet (corrosion, loose)? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||86SE||06-02-2000||02:11 PM||||Nope, havent checked the connections but it probibly wouldent be a bad idea.<P>It dident turn over super slow.  Slow enough to hear every stroke, and about 1-2 seconds for all 4 strokes.  Mabey that is super slow.<p>[This message has been edited by 86SE (edited 06-02-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||lennyb4||06-02-2000||02:25 PM||||Thats where i would start. Run you hand down the positive cable (firmly feeling) as far as you can to see if there might be a break in the line. Then check all the connections. Alot of time they will get corroded over time from water,salt,dirt, whatever. It might not be a bad idea to go ahead and check the ground while your at it.||||reg||6
Z||000004||JohnnyK||06-02-2000||03:25 PM||||My starter would turn mine over really slow, and no amount of cleaning would help it.. Got a new starter in there, and it turns over fast and fires up 300% quicker than before...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||86SE||06-02-2000||09:06 PM||||Remember when I said smoke was coming from the distributor??  It was coming from the starter!!  The smoke was coming from the starter, then coming up throught the other side of the motor leaking up around the distributor.<P>There wasent just a little smoke, it was a thick blanket.  I cant believe the starter still cranked!<P>I found a new one for $38 so i'll pick that up Monday.||||reg||11
